<p class="sst-lead">The Nyström approximation reconstructs the curve's scale operator \(P\) from \(n\) quadrature
nodes. Here the boundary is a pinched <strong>Cassini oval</strong>; slide \(n\) and watch the error to the true
operator collapse on <strong>log&ndash;log</strong> axes.</p>

<p>\[ \big\|P_n - P_\infty\big\|_F \longrightarrow 0 \quad\text{(spectrally, for analytic }\bm{c}). \]</p>

<div class="sst-frag">
  <p class="sst-note">The waist makes the Cassini harder than a round curve, yet the error still plunges far faster
  than the \(1/\sqrt{n}\) of Monte Carlo &mdash; what makes SST cheap enough for tens of thousands of shapes.</p>
</div>
